# Syntax: docs/LANGUAGE.md. Check with `rbb bid check`.
#
# The card-independent half of the catch that takes over once a trump suit
# is agreed. There are no auction patterns here: the rules key on
# `we.trump` and `we.forcing`, so the same rule serves a simple raise, a
# limit raise, a Jacoby 2NT, a splinter, a two-over-one and a transfer.
#
# The ask lives in blackwood.bid and rkcb-1430.bid, because which of them
# is active is a card question and the answers differ. The test that
# decides *whether* to ask is the same in both, and is written up in
# slam-catch.notes.md. When the card plays control bids, control-bids.bid
# runs first and this sign-off is what the dialogue falls back to.

module slam-catch "Game or slam once a trump suit is agreed"
  needs  base

# ── The sign-off ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Once a suit is agreed and we are forced to game, game in that suit is
# always a call we can fall back on. Nothing here says anything about the
# hand, so it ranks last: any rule with something to show beats it, and
# the slam tries above it beat it. It exists so that an auction which has
# agreed a trump suit never dies below game for want of a rule.

when we.trump is suit, we.forcing = game, !asked
  4{trump}  "Game in {trump}: nothing more to show"
            when trump is H | trump is S
            priority -20
